<title>USA: First Financial sees Q4 hurt by $4.4 mln.</title>
<headline>First Financial sees Q4 hurt by $4.4 mln.</headline>
<dateline>CHARLESTON, S.C. 1996-10-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>First Financial Holdings Inc said Tuesday that the Savings Association Insurance Fund provision will hurt fourth quarter after-tax earnings by about $4.4 million.</p>
<p>The provision was included in the omnibus appropriations package signed by President Clinton Monday.  </p>
<p>It said the $4.4 million estimate is based on an effective tax rate of 36.5 percent. The holding company also estimated that its thrift subsidiaries would expense about $2.6 million before taxes during fiscal 1996 for SAIF premiums.</p>
</text>
